  "details": "If your local avatar has a spotlight and it loads while your personal mirror is enabled, the spotlight appears brighter in the mirror clone than it does locally. Reloading the avatar, for example by toggling OSC, corrects the issue, and the spotlight then appears correctly in the mirror.\n\nWhile in the incorrect state, the spotlight also displays incorrectly in cameras, both in the mirror reflection and when viewing the local player through said camera. This issue is consistently reproducible and has been confirmed with other players, affecting all spotlights on avatars.\n\nThe mirrors original state does not seem to change the behaviour, and it happens to personal or world mirrors regardless of the layers being reflected.\n\nA fix for this would be appreciated as avatars should always appear true to their intended look, both in mirrors and cameras. Thank you!",
